{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "01", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "07", "M": "56", "S": "11"}}, "news": [{"title": "Andhra Pradesh set to pilot 3D-printed houses under PMAY-Gramin", "para": "The Andhra Pradesh government plans to leverage 3D printing technology for the construction of housing under PMAY-G. A project to build approximately 100 homes in Burripalem village is underway, with technical support from CBRI. Eligible beneficiaries will receive financial assistance between \u20b91.70 lakh and \u20b91.80 lakh. This cutting-edge technology is designed to greatly reduce both construction time and costs, while enhancing thermal comfort in the homes created.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/andhra-pradesh-set-to-pilot-3d-printed-houses-under-pmay-gramin/134610242?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-210470/134610242.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Indian design must absorb global influences without losing cultural identity: Sunita Kohli", "para": "Speaking at The Economic Times DesignScape Summit & Awards 2026, Padma Shri Sunita Kohli, President and Co-Founder, K2India, said contemporary Indian design should reinterpret global ideas through local craft, materials, climate and cultural knowledge rather than merely imitate international trends.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/indian-design-must-absorb-global-influences-without-losing-cultural-identity-sunita-kohli/134610503?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-71290/134610503.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Ahmedabad: Seven illegally constructed residential units in Fatehwadi razed", "para": "In a decisive move on Wednesday, the estate department of Ahmedabad Municipal Corporation took action against unauthorized construction by demolishing seven row houses in Fatehwadi. This followed a formal notice to property owners demanding the removal of illegal structures, which they ignored, prompting further action when the builder unlawfully resumed operations. Ultimately, the demolition eliminated over 7,100 square feet of violations.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/ahmedabad-seven-illegally-constructed-residential-units-in-fatehwadi-razed/134610187?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-308506/134610187.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}